# Files `wt step copy-ignored` may copy into a fresh worktree.
# A file must be BOTH gitignored AND listed here to be copied.
#
# `.worktreeinclude` itself is tracked; the files it names are copied at the
# filesystem level by `wt step copy-ignored` and are never staged (every path
# below is covered by .gitignore). Secrets therefore stay on disk, not in git.

# ── Machine-local state every parallel session needs ─────────────────────────

# Per-package environment files (live credentials — copied, never committed).
.env
.env.e2e
*.env.e2e

# Agent tooling config (MCP servers, editors) — same as the primary worktree.
.mcp.json
opencode.json
config/
.codex/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.goose/
.vscode/
.zed/

# Deploy runbook skill (gitignored; contains live deploy secrets — copied, not committed).
.claude/skills/deploy-travelcrm/

# ── Deliberately NOT copied ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules/    — 15 packages, no root workspace; install only what a session
#                    runs, or symlink the primary tree. A full copy is heavy and
#                    on ext4 there is no reflink.
# .gstack/         — browser-daemon runtime state; copying it fights the live daemon.
# .firebase/       — local Firebase deploy cache.
# env_backup/      — secret backups; no reason to duplicate them per worktree.
# Management/playwright-report/, test-results/ — test output, regenerate.
